# AI Coding System

Prefer the **user-global** rule `~/.cursor/rules/ai-coding-system-mcp.mdc` (applies in every project). This file is a short project copy of the same workflow.

## Session start

1. `register_project` or `get_project_context` (absolute workspace path). Continuing → `get_handoff`.
2. `compression_guidance` (Caveman terse replies).
3. Do not re-ask known architecture / handoff.

## Per task

1. If unsure which ACS tool to call → `decide_tools` (Von), then call only the recommended tool.
2. `prepare_context` (memory/graph opt-in only).
3. `discipline_rules`; `security_refs` when security-relevant.
4. Large I/O → Context Mode (`ctx_execute` / `ctx_execute_file` / `ctx_search`). History → Mem 3-layer search.
5. Structure → Graphify tools via ACS, not full-repo dumps.
6. Owned running UI → Reticle peer MCP after `decide_tools` returns `reticle_verify` (or call `reticle_guidance`).
7. Next.js content/pages → `seo_guidance` with user keywords; install `next-seo` in the app and ship SEO with the content (not later).

## Task complete

`update_handoff` / `finalize_task`. Quality/security scans at boundaries only.

## Token discipline

No full repo/file pastes. No every-tool-every-turn. Prefer handoff over full context when continuing.
